# Go tooling writes LF and gofmt treats CRLF files as unformatted. Without this, every Go file in
# a Windows working tree is reported by `gofmt -l`, which buries genuine formatting problems in
# noise and makes the CI check impossible to reproduce locally.
*.go text eol=lf
*.mod text eol=lf
*.sum text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
